# JARVIS - BLUEPRINT

Put this file at `docs/BLUEPRINT.md`. Antigravity reads it before every task.
As-of date for all model and pricing facts: 2026-11-05. Re-verify before relying on them.

## 1. How we win

One user, one machine. Success means the four must-haves work live, measurably:
1. FULL-DUPLEX VOICE with barge-in: interrupt mid-sentence, speech stops <= 200 ms, Jarvis keeps what it had said, answers the interruption.
2. TASKS BY VOICE, starting with WhatsApp, behind a mandatory spoken confirmation gate.
3. BROWSER AWARENESS: sees the current tab and explains it in context, with a strict never-shared list.
4. TUTOR MODE: L0-L4 explanations, learner memory, quizzes, spaced repetition.

Edge, in order: (1) measured latency, logged every turn; (2) a safety layer (tiers, gate, audit, kill phrase) so a misheard word never sends a wrong message; (3) a startup health check that fails loudly when Google retires a model; (4) a cost guard so a forgotten open session cannot surprise you; (5) a voice layer behind an interface so the model or provider can be swapped.

## 2. Product shape

A background desktop daemon (Windows-first, tray icon) plus a Chrome Manifest V3 extension. The extension is the browser sensor and its side panel is the UI. A website alone is rejected: a page cannot run in the background, read other tabs, or drive WhatsApp.

