## 6. Voice loop spec

Audio: 16 kHz mono PCM16 in, 24 kHz out (confirm in the Live docs during P1), frames of 20-32 ms.

Barge-in sequence (budget 200 ms total, headphones):
1. mic frame -> VAD says speech (target <= 40 ms from onset, needs 2 consecutive speech frames).
2. state SPEAKING -> INTERRUPTED; stop the output stream and clear the playback queue (<= 1 frame).
3. send the cancel signal to the provider (do not wait for the server's `interrupted` event).
4. compute `spoken_fraction = played_samples / generated_samples`; truncate the assistant transcript to that fraction at a word boundary; save as `{role: assistant, interrupted: true, text: truncated}`.
5. keep streaming the user's audio so their interruption is heard; go to LISTENING.
6. context: if the provider does not retain what was said, inject a short note "[you were cut off after: ...]". Which case applies is UNVERIFIED; P2 tests it.

Metrics per turn (logs/latency.jsonl): `turn_id, state_times{...}, time_to_first_audio_ms, barge_in_to_silence_ms (software, plus measured device latency), end_of_speech_to_response_ms, interrupted, spoken_fraction`.

Echo: headphones first. `AEC_ENABLED=true` adds the AEC stage. Without AEC in speaker mode: raise the VAD threshold and require about 250 ms of continuous speech before cutting (slower barge-in, fewer self-interrupts).

Idle timeout: close the cloud session after `SESSION_IDLE_TIMEOUT_S` of no speech (default 120) to stop input billing.

## 7. Models and health check

Config keys (values live only in `.env`; defaults below are what `.env.example` ships on 2026-11-05):

| Key | Purpose | Example value |
|---|---|---|
| GEMINI_API_KEY | key from a billing-enabled Google Cloud project | (secret) |
| GEMINI_LIVE_MODEL | voice | gemini-3.8-live |
| GEMINI_TEXT_MODEL | planning, tutoring, quizzes, perception | gemini-3.8-flash |
| OLLAMA_MODEL | offline brain | qwen3:4b or llama3.1:8b |
| OLLAMA_EMBED_MODEL | embeddings | nomic-embed-text |
| STT_LOCAL_MODEL, TTS_LOCAL_VOICE | local pipeline | faster-whisper size, Piper voice name |

Startup health check (`core/brain/health.py`, also `python -m jarvis doctor`):
1. list models from the Gemini API with the key;
2. confirm both configured Gemini models are in the list;
3. open a 2-second test Live session with `GEMINI_LIVE_MODEL`, send 1 s of silence, expect a clean open and close;
4. confirm the Ollama model is pulled;
5. on any failure: print and speak a message naming the exact retired or missing model and the fix ("GEMINI_LIVE_MODEL=gemini-3.1-flash-live-preview is retired. Set GEMINI_LIVE_MODEL in .env, then restart."), exit non-zero for cloud mode, and offer offline mode. Never fail silently.

Verified against Google on 2026-11-05 (sources below):
- gemini-2.0-flash and -001: shut down 1 Jun 2026. gemini-2.0-flash-live-001: shut down 9 Dec 2025 (this is what the old planner.py used).
- gemini-3.1-flash-live-preview and gemini-2.5-flash-native-audio-preview-12-2025: shut down 17 Nov 2026; replacement gemini-3.8-live.
- gemini-2.5-flash/-pro/-flash-lite: Google lists "no shutdown date announced". Your tracker's 16 Oct 2026 date is NOT confirmed on Google's page. Do not depend on 2.5.
- Live pricing (paid): audio in $3.00 per 1M tokens = $0.005/min; audio out $12.00 per 1M = $0.018/min. Free tier: content may be used to improve Google products; paid tier: not.
- Text: gemini-3.8-flash $0.75 in / $3.75 out per 1M tokens through 31 Dec 2026, then $1.50 / $7.50. gemini-3.5-flash-lite $0.30 / $2.50.
- LiveKit docs: plugin default model is still the 2.5 native-audio preview (dies 17 Nov), so any LiveKit use must pass the model explicitly.
Sources: ai.google.dev/gemini-api/docs/deprecations, ai.google.dev/gemini-api/docs/pricing, docs.livekit.io/agents/models/realtime/plugins/gemini/, pypi.org/project/livekit-plugins-google.
