## 8. Cost guard

Meter audio seconds actually sent and received (not wall-clock), per session, persisted in SQLite (`cost_events`).
Rates from config: `GEMINI_LIVE_IN_USD_PER_MIN=0.005`, `GEMINI_LIVE_OUT_USD_PER_MIN=0.018`, text rates per 1M tokens with an effective date.
Budget: `GEMINI_MONTHLY_BUDGET_USD` (required), optional `GEMINI_DAILY_BUDGET_USD`. At 80%: speak a warning once and log. At 100%: close the session, switch to offline mode, say so; stays offline until the next period or a manual override.
Worked estimate (owner's arithmetic from the rates above, 12 spoken min per hour): continuous mic 60 x 0.005 + 12 x 0.018 = about $0.52/h; gated mic (stream about 20% of the time) about $0.28/h; an open session left 24 h costs about $7.20/day input alone, hence the idle timeout.
The estimate can drift from Google's bill. The owner also sets a Cloud Billing budget alert.

## 9. Privacy

| Data | Cloud model | Rule |
|---|---|---|
| Your spoken audio | goes to Google while cloud Live is active | WhatsApp recipient and body use local private capture instead |
| WhatsApp bodies, contact lists | never | local only, unless per-session opt-in `--allow-cloud-messages` |
| Page text on a denylisted domain | never | host only, or redacted, or routed to Ollama |
| Page text elsewhere | allowed after the "explain this page" intent | capped at 20,000 chars, wrapped as untrusted |
| Incognito tabs, password fields, form values | never | extension drops them |
| Logs | never contain bodies, secrets, page text | hash plus length only |

`config/denylist.yaml` ships with banking, email (Gmail, Outlook, Proton), password managers (1Password, Bitwarden, LastPass), health and tax portals; the owner extends it.

